geanycli
========

A Geany plugin that provides tabbed VTE terminals inside the message window.

Features
--------
- "Cli" tab added to the Geany message window
- Multiple terminal tabs, each running $SHELL at the project root
- New tab button (+) in the tab bar; close (×) button on each tab
- Minimum one terminal is always kept open
- Shell is restarted automatically if it exits
- Inter-plugin IPC: other plugins can request commands to be run

Inter-plugin IPC
----------------
Two equivalent methods are available:

1. GLib signal (no header required):

     g_signal_emit_by_name(geany->object, "geanycli-run-command", "make", FALSE);

2. Direct function call via GModule symbol lookup:

     typedef void (*GtRunCmdFn)(const gchar *, gboolean);
     GtRunCmdFn fn;
     if (g_module_symbol(terminal_plugin->module, "geanycli_run_command", gpointer *)&fn)) 
         fn("make", FALSE);

Parameters:
  cmd     – shell command string to execute
  new_tab – TRUE  : open a new terminal tab then run cmd
            FALSE : run cmd in the currently active terminal tab

Requirements
------------
- GTK+ >= 3.0
- VTE >= 0.48 (vte-2.91)
- Geany >= 2.1

Known Issues
------------
None currently known.

